"""Copy for the AI site routing screen, and for a render that failed.

Why the AI screen exists
------------------------
A Cloudflare Worker cannot open a socket to a Cloudflare owned address. ChatGPT,
Claude and Perplexity all sit behind Cloudflare, so a direct connection from
inside the worker fails outright and the site simply never loads: the classic
"everything works except ChatGPT" report. The fix is to send those destinations
through a relay, and to send them through the *same* relay every time so the site
sees one steady exit address instead of a different Cloudflare datacentre on every
request, which is what triggers the endless re-logins and "unusual activity"
checks.

``wg.render_failed`` exists because the old delivery path swallowed its own
exceptions. A user who taps a button and receives nothing cannot tell a broken bot
from a cold pool.
"""

